# Closed kan (ankan) reveals its kan dora IMMEDIATELY before the replacement draw,
# so a Rinshan Kaihou tsumo counts the new kan dora (engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17).
# Also confirms own ankan cancels ippatsu (rules.md §4.26).
# Seat 0 declares Double Riichi on turn 1 (holding 234m 678p 56s 999m 88p),
# draws 4th 9m on turn 2, declares ankan 9m -> kan dora 8m (-> dora 9m, +4 dora!) flips immediately,
# draws rinshan 7s and wins by tsumo!
# Scoring for Seat 0 (dealer, East):
#   Hand: 234m 678p 56s 88p + ankan 9999m + rinshan tsumo 7s
#   Yaku: double_riichi (2) + tsumo (1) + rinshan (1) + dora:4 (9m x4 from kan dora 8m) = 8 han (Baiman).
#   (NO ippatsu: own ankan cancelled it. Dora indicators: 1z -> 2z, 8m -> 9m. Ura: 5z -> 6z, 5z -> 6z.)
#   Fu: 20 base + 2 tsumo + 32 ankan(9m) = 54 -> 60 fu.
#   Dealer tsumo Baiman = 8000 all (+24000 from opponents; recovers own 1000 stick -> net +24000).
#   Deltas: +24000 -8000 -8000 -8000.

[meta]
name: closed_kan_rinshan_tsumo
title: Closed kan reveals kan dora immediately for Rinshan tsumo and cancels own ippatsu
rules: mahjongsoul
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §4.26

